{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvacYF6txb3h4jNBj11p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**My recommendation: don't scale it, and don't let a non-buyer survey hold up the decision. The test has already answered the main question: this offer doesn't work as designed.**\n\n**What the numbers show**\n- 0.3% of 20,000 is about 60 buyers. About 24 asked for refunds, leaving roughly 36 retained, or 0.18%. That's about 17 times below the 3% target, bringing in around £540 a month.\n- A price cut won't close a gap that size. Even if halving the price tripled uptake, which would be unusually strong, you'd still be far short and earning less per customer.\n- The 40% refund rate is the most important signal. People who did value it enough to pay mostly decided it wasn't worth it. That points to the product or what was promised, not the price.\n\n**Why the survey is the wrong tool**\n- People are poor at predicting what they would pay. \"Would you buy at £8?\" overstates real demand.\n- Most non-buyers probably don't want premium support at any price, so the survey would mostly measure indifference.\n\n**What to do instead (cheap, uses data you already have)**\n1. **Talk to the ~60 buyers, especially the ~24 who asked for refunds.** Find out what they expected and what fell short. This is your richest source.\n2. **Compare treatment and control** on churn, satisfaction scores and contacts to standard support. Check whether the offer annoyed customers, or implied that standard support is worse.\n3. **Check exposure.** Confirm customers actually saw and understood the offer before blaming demand.\n\nIf that work turns up a clear, fixable gap in what's offered, redesign the product and run a real randomised price test with actual purchases. Otherwise, stop and move the effort elsewhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3186,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3186},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e2840d9-a326-40cc-ae96-19e661315480","uuid":"06350082-81af-416b-ad61-72345d14c8a2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:07:53.875Z","request_id":"req_011CfvacXzDxKGUEKWDp54uG"}
